# OpenDB

#C#Knowledge#= **OpenDB** is a free database of articles, media and papers that anyone can reuse. Everything in it is **CC0**, which means public domain!

[Open OpenDB](/opendb) · [Phone version](/opendb/mobile/)


::divider{wavy|OpenDB|red}
## Entries

An entry is a `.kd` file: a header with an id, type, title and tags, and then Keydown text. Types include #T.bubble(article), #T.bubble(image), #T.bubble(paper) and #T.bubble(lite)!

```
---
format: keydown-text
id: my-article
type: article
title: My article
summary: One sentence about it.
tags: [example]
license: CC0-1.0
---
**My article** is about something. Link to another entry like [[keydown|Keydown]]!
```

## Wiki links

`[[id|words]]` links to another entry. The Keydown guide and the Radii Office article are entries too!

## Lites

A #G.bubble(lite) is a small, runnable project stored as one entry (like a Gist). Each file sits in a `~~~ file:` fence. You can #G.bubble(fork), #G.bubble(embed) and #G.bubble(zip) a lite!

## Every example is live

OpenDB draws its pages with the real Keydown engine, so every example in an article is the real thing, not a picture!

## Reuse

Because it is CC0, you can copy anything from OpenDB into your own project without asking. It is also where the full [Keydown article](#/keydown-reference) lives, and the docs here read it directly!
